It reads open data published by the U.S. National Aeronautics and Space
Administration (NASA):
  - the Near Earth Object Web Service (NeoWs) of api.nasa.gov, data of the
    JPL Center for Near Earth Object Studies (CNEOS);
  - the images of the Earth Polychromatic Imaging Camera (EPIC) on board the
    NOAA DSCOVR spacecraft, at https://epic.gsfc.nasa.gov/;
  - the Earth Observatory Natural Event Tracker (EONET) v3, at
    https://eonet.gsfc.nasa.gov/, which aggregates other sources (GDACS,
    IRWIN, JTWC, NATICE, Smithsonian GVP…).
NASA content is generally not subject to copyright in the United States; the
integration credits NASA as the source. This integration is not affiliated
with nor endorsed by NASA, and uses neither its name as a brand nor its
insignia ("meatball", "worm") or any other NASA emblem.

The test fixtures under test/fixtures/nasa/ are answers of those services
downloaded on 2026-11-05.
